From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Catti-Schmidt <kschmi@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:07:27 -0700
Subject: [svg] Fall back to masking when SVG clip path union fails

LayoutSVGResourceClipper::AsPath() combines multiple <clipPath> children
using SkOpBuilder. If the union failed, Blink ignored the failure and
cached the first child as a valid analytic clip. Painting then used only
that child, while hit testing and clip bounds continued to account for
every child, producing inconsistent rendering and interaction geometry.

Handle union failure by leaving the analytic-path cache invalid and
returning std::nullopt. This invokes the existing mask-based fallback,
which paints every contributing child and keeps painting consistent with
hit testing and intersection geometry. Use the modern
std::optional<SkPath> -returning SkOpBuilder::resolve() API rather than
its deprecated output-parameter overload.

Add a WPT reftest covering HTML and SVG clip-path consumers. It uses a
valid path ending in a trailing moveto, which causes Skia path-union
resolution to fail, and verifies that all clip-path children still
contribute to the rendered clip. Verified that the new WPT passes in
Firefox as well.

Bug: 574376000
Change-Id: Ia07a8bbcde4e776b7ff576622fef57a7232fab2e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8608391
Reviewed-by: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt <kschmi@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722404}

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/svg/layout_svg_resource_clipper.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/svg/layout_svg_resource_clipper.cc
index deb3a721543e12740361ac2dcbaa37dcb2918b8e..8670961818d6f80c4302eff8f1d0f156f5a76d6c 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/svg/layout_svg_resource_clipper.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/svg/layout_svg_resource_clipper.cc
@@ -168,8 +168,13 @@ std::optional<Path> LayoutSVGResourceClipper::AsPath() {
     }
   }
 
-  if (clip_path_builder)
-    clip_path_builder->resolve(&resolved_path);
+  if (clip_path_builder) {
+    std::optional<SkPath> path = clip_path_builder->resolve();
+    if (!path) {
+      return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    resolved_path = std::move(*path);
+  }
   clip_content_path_ = std::move(resolved_path);
   clip_content_path_validity_ = kClipContentPathValid;
   return std::optional<Path>(clip_content_path_);
